         "id": "SECTION_prerequisites",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Prerequisites\n\nThis game reinforces the text *Advancing an Order and the Complement* (<htcite0>). Read that text first: it explains that the complement of a digit to 10 is the limit — adding a value smaller than the complement keeps the column, and adding the complement or more makes it advance to the next order.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "cabc9843-35ef-4e4f-92fd-17eda864b55e",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Advancing an Order and the Complement",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_game",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Game\n\nAt every order — units, tens, hundreds and thousands — we ask the same question: when we add a digit to the digit already in the column, does the column carry 1 to the next order (<htcite0>)?\n\nThe answer is decided by the complement to 10. The complement of the digit already in the column is the value that completes 10. If the digit we add is smaller than the complement, the sum stays below 10 and there is no carry. If we add the complement or more, the sum reaches 10 and the column carries 1.\n\nLook at the two digits, choose **Carry** or **Not carry**, and the game will explain the result and show the squares of the complement to 10. There are four levels: units, tens, hundreds and thousands.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "648fb7b4-ba73-452e-980b-6d68d57d16b9",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Our current numbers",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<div class=\"htCarryGame\"><span class=\"htCarryLevel\" id=\"htCarryLevel\"></span><div class=\"htCarryOrders\" id=\"htCarryOrders\"></div><span class=\"htCarryQuestion\" id=\"htCarryQuestion\"></span><table class=\"htCarryTable\" aria-live=\"polite\"><tr class=\"htCarryCarryRow\"><td class=\"htCarryOp\"></td><td class=\"htCarryTens\"><span id=\"htCarryCarryValue\" class=\"htCarryCarryValue\"></span></td><td class=\"htCarryUnits\"></td></tr><tr><td class=\"htCarryOp\"></td><td class=\"htCarryTens\"></td><td class=\"htCarryUnits\" id=\"htCarryFirst\">0</td></tr><tr><td class=\"htCarryOp\">+</td><td class=\"htCarryTens\"></td><td class=\"htCarryUnits\" id=\"htCarryAddend\">0</td></tr><tr class=\"htCarryLine\"><td colspan=\"3\"></td></tr><tr><td class=\"htCarryOp\"></td><td class=\"htCarryTens\" id=\"htCarryTensResult\"></td><td class=\"htCarryUnits\" id=\"htCarryUnitsResult\"></td></tr></table><div class=\"htCarryButtonsRow\"><button type=\"button\" id=\"htCarryBtn\" class=\"htCarryButton\">Carry</button><button type=\"button\" id=\"htCarryNotBtn\" class=\"htCarryButton\">Not carry</button></div><div class=\"htCarryFeedback\" id=\"htCarryFeedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div><div class=\"htCarrySquaresWrap htCarryHidden\" id=\"htCarrySquaresWrap\"><span class=\"htCarrySquaresLabel\" id=\"htCarrySquaresLabel\">Complement to 10</span><div class=\"htCarrySquares\" id=\"htCarrySquares\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div><span class=\"htCarrySquaresCaption\" id=\"htCarrySquaresCaption\"></span></div><div class=\"htCarryNextContainer\"><button type=\"button\" id=\"htCarryNextBtn\" class=\"reset-tutor-btn hidden\">Next level</button></div><span id=\"htCarryLevelTemplate\" class=\"htCarryHidden\">Level {n} of 4</span><span id=\"htCarryQuestionTemplate\" class=\"htCarryHidden\">Does the {order} order carry 1 to the next order?</span><span id=\"htCarryOrder0\" class=\"htCarryHidden\">Units</span><span id=\"htCarryOrder1\" class=\"htCarryHidden\">Tens</span><span id=\"htCarryOrder2\" class=\"htCarryHidden\">Hundreds</span><span id=\"htCarryOrder3\" class=\"htCarryHidden\">Thousands</span><span id=\"htCarryNextLabel\" class=\"htCarryHidden\">Next level</span><span id=\"htCarryPlayAgainLabel\" class=\"htCarryHidden\">Play again</span><span id=\"htCarryMsgCarryCorrect\" class=\"htCarryHidden\">Correct! The complement of {first} to 10 is {comp}. Since {addend} is equal to or greater than {comp}, {first} + {addend} = {sum} reaches 10, so the {order} order carries 1 to the next order.</span><span id=\"htCarryMsgNotCorrect\" class=\"htCarryHidden\">Correct! The complement of {first} to 10 is {comp}. Since {addend} is less than {comp}, {first} + {addend} = {sum} stays below 10, so the {order} order does not carry.</span><span id=\"htCarryMsgCarryWrong\" class=\"htCarryHidden\">Not yet. The complement of {first} to 10 is {comp}. Since {addend} is less than {comp}, {first} + {addend} = {sum} stays below 10. The {order} order does not carry.</span><span id=\"htCarryMsgNotWrong\" class=\"htCarryHidden\">Not yet. The complement of {first} to 10 is {comp}. Since {addend} is equal to or greater than {comp}, {first} + {addend} = {sum} reaches 10. The {order} order carries 1 to the next order.</span></div>",
